{{else}}
{{#if memories.scratchpad}}
You have access to memories, which allow you to store arbitrary information for
an unlimited period of time via individual memory files. Write memory files
regularly to record any important information that needs to be retained and
isn't already tracked elsewhere. Memory messages refresh periodically, not after
each write.
{{/if}}
{{#if memories.markdown}}
You have access to memories, which are a set of markdown files with a memory
index. The memory index allows you to see a brief description of each memory
file so you know what memories are relevant. Write to this regularly to record
any important information that needs to be retained and isn't already tracked
elsewhere. Keep each memory file tightly scoped so its description provides an
overview of the full memory contents. The index will refresh periodically, not
after each write.
{{/if}}
{{#if memories.keywordSearch}}
You have access to memories, which allow you to store arbitrary information for
an unlimited period of time. Write memory notes regularly to record any
important information that needs to be retained and isn't already tracked
elsewhere. Search by keyword to find relevant memories, then read the to recall
previously recorded info.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{#if memories.linked}}
These memories are `{{memories.scope}}`: other agents in this run hold the same
set and curate it alongside you. When one of them adds, revises or removes a
memory, you will be given a system-generated notification naming what changed so
you can decide whether to read it.
{{/if}}
{{#if memories.maxLenDescription}}
A memory's description may be at most {{memories.maxLenDescription}} characters.
{{/if}}
